{"checked":"2026-11-14T11:03Z","warnings":[{"id":"IDQ20827","title":"Minor Flood Warning for the Upper Condamine River","issued":"Issued at 11:43 am AEST on Saturday 14 November 2026","text":"IDQ20827\nAustralian Government Bureau of Meteorology\n\nMinor Flood Warning for the Upper Condamine River\n\nIssued at 11:43 am AEST on Saturday 14 November 2026\nFlood Warning Number: 2\n\n\nMINOR FLOODING OCCURRING AT TUMMAVILLE\n\nThunderstorms have produced heavy rainfall since Friday afternoon in parts of the Upper\nCondamine River catchment.  River and creek levels are rising and isolated flooding is\noccurring. Minor flooding is occurring at Tummaville.\n\nFurther rainfall is forecast over the Upper Condamine catchment in the next few days.\n\nCondamine River downstream of Warwick to Oakey Creek:\nMinor flooding is occurring at Tummaville. Minor flooding is continuing along Hodgson\nCreek at Felton and along the Condamine River at Millbrook.\n\nThe Condamine River at Tummaville is currently at 5.66 m and rising, with minor flooding.\nThe Condamine River at Tummaville is likely to remain above the minor flood level (5.00 m)\nSaturday into Sunday. The river may peak near 5.70 m Saturday afternoon, with minor\nflooding.\n\nSafety Advice:\n* Don't drive, walk, swim or play in floodwater because it is dangerous.\n* Stay away from flooded drains, rivers, streams and waterways.\n* Obey road closure signs. Plan ahead so you don't drive on flooded roads.\n* Check the ABC and local media for updates. The situation can change quickly, so stay\ninformed.\n* For local emergency management warnings and advice visit\nwww.disaster.qld.gov.au/warnings.\n\nFor emergency assistance call SES on telephone number 132 500. In life-threatening\nemergencies, call 000 (triple zero) immediately.\n\nNext issue:\nThe next warning will be issued by 03:00 PM AEST on Sunday 15 November 2026.\n\nLatest River Heights:\nLocation                                    River Height   Tendency Time of Observation\nCondamine River at The Head                   2.11 m       Steady   10:08 am Sat 14/11/26\nSpring Creek at Killarney Alert               1.38 m       Steady   10:34 am Sat 14/11/26\nCondamine River at Killarney                  0.65 m       Steady   8:54 am Sat 14/11/26\nCondamine River at Elbow Valley               1.01 m       Steady   11:00 am Sat 14/11/26\nCondamine River at Murrays Bridge             1.83 m       Steady   8:43 am Sat 14/11/26\nConnolly Dam                                  0.13 m       Rising   9:46 am Sat 14/11/26\nCondamine River at Warwick                    1.69 m       Falling  11:25 am Sat 14/11/26\nSandy Creek at Leslie Dam HG                -1.84 mAHD     Steady   11:00 am Sat 14/11/26\nGlengallan Creek                              1.55 m       Falling  11:28 am Sat 14/11/26\nCondamine River at Pratten                    1.42 m       Steady   9:17 am Sat 14/11/26\nDalrymple Creek at Allora                     2.04 m       Rising   11:00 am Sat 14/11/26\nCondamine River at Millbrook                  4.91 m       Falling  11:26 am Sat 14/11/26\nCondamine River at Tummaville                 5.66 m       Rising   11:20 am Sat 14/11/26\nCondamine River at Centenary Bridge          4.56 mAHD     Rising   10:48 am Sat 14/11/26\nCondamine River at Cecil Plains               3.89 m       Steady   11:00 am Sat 14/11/26\nOakey Creek at Jondaryan                      0.37 m       Steady   11:00 am Sat 14/11/26\nOakey Creek at Fairview                       0.52 m       Steady   11:00 am Sat 14/11/26\n\nThis advice is also available by dialling 1300 659 219. Warning, rainfall and river\ninformation are available at http://www.bom.gov.au/australia/flood.\n\nCopyright Commonwealth of Australia 2011, Bureau of Meteorology (ABN 92 637 533\n532).  Users of these web pages are deemed to have read and accepted the\nconditions described in the Copyright, Disclaimer, and Privacy statements\n(http://www.bom.gov.au/other/copyright.shtml).\n"}],"rivers":{"pr